1
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:08,033
Stockroom tracks workshop parts, shelf locations and every stock movement.

2
00:00:08,033 --> 00:00:14,433
Search narrows the inventory by item name or SKU.

3
00:00:14,433 --> 00:00:21,800
Stock filters separate low inventory from items that are completely out of stock.

4
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:25,600
New items start at zero stock. Receipts and issues change the balance through the ledger.

5
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:34,433
A Torx bit set is added with a unique SKU, a shelf location and a reorder threshold.

6
00:00:34,433 --> 00:00:37,867
A receipt records both the quantity and its reference.

7
00:00:37,867 --> 00:00:45,233
Receiving five units updates the balance and creates a permanent movement record.

8
00:00:45,233 --> 00:00:50,000
The item detail connects its current balance to its transaction history.

9
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:55,967
Item details can change without rewriting the stock history.

10
00:00:55,967 --> 00:01:00,600
The shelf changes from D-04 to D-05; the five-unit balance stays unchanged.

11
00:01:00,600 --> 00:01:04,433
An issue removes units and records the reason. The resulting balance is shown before saving.

12
00:01:04,433 --> 00:01:11,800
All five units are issued to the workshop, bringing the item back to zero.

13
00:01:11,800 --> 00:01:16,533
Only a zero-stock item can be archived. Its receipts and issues remain recorded.

14
00:01:16,533 --> 00:01:20,133
The item is archived after its stock reaches zero.

15
00:01:20,133 --> 00:01:26,600
Archiving removes the item from active inventory without deleting its history.

16
00:01:28,800 --> 00:01:36,167
Commit 388acdf made the inventory heading follow the selected stock filter.

17
00:01:36,167 --> 00:01:44,367
Tests, scans and image publishing passed. Deployment to EKS used a manual Helm upgrade.

18
00:01:44,367 --> 00:01:50,733
The container image is tagged with the full source commit SHA.

19
00:01:50,733 --> 00:01:58,100
Helm revision 2 and the health response identify the same published commit.

20
00:01:58,100 --> 00:02:04,500
The deployed stock filter now displays the corrected Low stock heading.

21
00:02:06,700 --> 00:02:16,233
Live local Kubernetes metrics: 22,584 successful reads, zero failures, and scaling from two replicas to five.

22
00:02:16,233 --> 00:02:23,067
Prometheus discovers the backend replicas and scrapes their metrics successfully.

23
00:02:25,267 --> 00:02:30,433
The EKS cluster runs in the Mumbai region.

24
00:02:30,433 --> 00:02:35,567
The managed node group contains two worker nodes.

25
00:02:35,567 --> 00:02:43,533
Terraform destroy removed all 34 managed resources. The EKS cluster list is empty.
